# `AutomataflLegCGolden` — the BYTE-PINNED wire goldens for the Leg C descriptor (M1)

`AutomataflLegCEmit` authors the Leg C AIR as an `n`-parametric family and pins its SHAPE. This file
pins its BYTES: `emitVmJson2 (automataflLegCDescN n)` at the DEPLOYED size `n = 11` (553 KiB) and at
the canary size `n = 5` (153 KiB), the board the rules file's own fork/collide audit witnesses live
on. Any change to a gate, a column index, a PI base or the emission order breaks these `#guard`s.

## Why a separate leaf

The goldens are large and mechanical; keeping them out of the authored file keeps that file readable.
This is exactly the split `AutomataflNGenGolden` makes for Leg R (`step ≈ 858 KiB`,
`resolve ≈ 1.3 MiB`). Imports are read-only; nothing here defines AIR.

Unlike Leg R — whose `automataflResolveDescN n` hard-codes the `n2` name for EVERY `n`, forcing
`AutomataflNGenGolden` to carry `.name`-patching wrappers — `automataflLegCDescN` computes its name
from `n`, so these are the descriptors themselves, not wrappers around them.

NOT registered in `EmitByName.lean` and NOT on disk under `circuit/descriptors/by-name/`: that is M4
(the witness generator lands with the registration, so a registered descriptor is never one nothing
can fill).
